WEBVTT

00:00:10.015 --> 00:00:19.719
Chapter 7 A terrible year 1992 was a very bad year for the royal family.

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:26.402
In January, holiday photographs of Fergie and Steve Wyatt appeared in the newspapers.

00:00:26.462 --> 00:00:29.132
The British people were shocked.

00:00:29.192 --> 00:00:32.643
Fergie's marriage to Prince Andrew was finished.

00:00:32.703 --> 00:00:35.233
Wyatt went back to America.

00:00:35.293 --> 00:00:40.464
Then Fergie became friends with an American called John Bryan.

00:00:40.524 --> 00:00:45.066
In February, Charles and Diana went to India.

00:00:45.126 --> 00:00:49.776
Photographers took pictures of Diana in front of the Taj Mahal.

00:00:49.836 --> 00:00:53.557
The history of the Taj Mahal is very romantic.

00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:57.218
An Indian emperor built it for his dead wife.

00:00:57.278 --> 00:01:00.622
Diana sat in front of it alone.

00:01:00.682 --> 00:01:04.324
Charles was at a business meeting.

00:01:04.384 --> 00:01:10.800
On the 29th of March Diana's father, Johnny, died suddenly.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:15.463
Diana was on a skiing holiday with Charles and the boys in Austria.

00:01:15.523 --> 00:01:18.956
Her father's death was a terrible shock.

00:01:19.016 --> 00:01:22.517
Charles and Diana flew back to London.

00:01:22.577 --> 00:01:32.732
On the 1st of April, Diana drove to all thought for the funeral, the ceremony for a dead person, and Charles came later by helicopter.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:41.156
Diana did not like Rain, Johnny's wife, but at the funeral she spoke to Rain and held her hand.

00:01:41.216 --> 00:01:46.068
After this, Diana's relationship with Rain was better.

00:01:46.128 --> 00:01:50.203
Andrew Morton's book about Diana was ready.

00:01:50.263 --> 00:01:55.126
He called it Diana, her true story.

00:01:55.186 --> 00:02:00.077
Diana wanted the British people to know the truth about her life.

00:02:00.137 --> 00:02:02.707
But now she was worried.

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:06.418
The royal family did not know anything about the book.

00:02:06.478 --> 00:02:10.048
Perhaps the book was not a good idea.

00:02:10.108 --> 00:02:18.431
On the 7th of June, 1992, the Sunday Times newspaper printed a part of Andrew Morton's book.

00:02:18.491 --> 00:02:22.976
For the first time, people read about Diana's bulimia.

00:02:23.035 --> 00:02:25.868
They read about Charles and Camilla.

00:02:25.928 --> 00:02:29.802
They learned how Charles was cold to Diana.

00:02:29.861 --> 00:02:33.956
Now people could not believe in the royal fairy story.

00:02:34.016 --> 00:02:36.497
They were very shocked.

00:02:36.557 --> 00:02:40.572
The British people began to dislike Prince Charles.

00:02:40.632 --> 00:02:46.029
Charles is a bad husband and not a very good father, they said.

00:02:46.089 --> 00:02:52.739
He doesn't care about Diana, he only cares about himself and Camilla Parker Bowles.

00:02:52.798 --> 00:02:56.472
The royal family asked questions.

00:02:56.532 --> 00:03:00.756
Andrew Morton did not write this book alone, they said.

00:03:00.816 --> 00:03:03.648
So Diana's friends talked to him.

00:03:03.708 --> 00:03:07.411
But did Diana know about this book?

00:03:07.471 --> 00:03:14.775
The husband of Diana's sister Jane was Robert Fellows, private secretary to the Queen.

00:03:14.835 --> 00:03:18.034
Did you know about Andrew Morton's book?

00:03:18.094 --> 00:03:19.996
He asked Diana.

00:03:20.056 --> 00:03:23.478
No, replied Diana.

00:03:23.538 --> 00:03:28.950
Fellows believed her, but later he found out the truth.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:33.593
Diana became more popular because of Andrew Morton's book.

00:03:33.653 --> 00:03:39.306
At the end of June 1992, she went to Belfast in Northern Ireland.

00:03:39.366 --> 00:03:44.580
We want die, we want die, shouted the people.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:54.446
In August 1992, the Sun newspaper printed stories about Diana and James Gilby, and Diana and James Hewitt.

00:03:54.506 --> 00:04:00.732
Later, Diana and Charles went to Korea, but the visit was not successful.

00:04:00.791 --> 00:04:04.144
Charles and Diana did not look happy together.

00:04:04.204 --> 00:04:08.707
In November, Diana went to Paris alone.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:13.052
The problems between Charles and Diana grew worse.

00:04:13.112 --> 00:04:20.241
On 25 November, they met at Kensington Palace and talked about a separation.

00:04:20.301 --> 00:04:27.438
On 9 December, the Prime Minister John Major gave a speech to the British Parliament.

00:04:27.498 --> 00:04:36.598
The Prince and Princess of Wales have decided to separate, he said, but they had no plans to divorce.

00:04:36.658 --> 00:04:51.270
In her Christmas speech at the end of the year, the Queen called 1992 a horrible year for the royal family.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:05:07.972
Chapter 8 Princess Alone Diana was now alone, and she wanted a normal private life.

00:05:08.032 --> 00:05:13.480
Because she was the Princess of Wales, she had a policeman with her all the time.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:18.054
But now Diana decided she did not need a policeman.

00:05:18.114 --> 00:05:24.910
Without a policeman, it was easy for the newspaper reporters and photographers to follow her.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.564
They waited for her outside Kensington Palace.

00:05:28.624 --> 00:05:31.976
They waited for her when she went out in London.

00:05:32.036 --> 00:05:36.768
They waited for her at airports when she went on holiday.

00:05:36.828 --> 00:05:43.190
Diana's sons, Prince William and Prince Harry, were the center of her life.

00:05:43.249 --> 00:05:45.981
Diana was a very good mother.

00:05:46.041 --> 00:05:56.696
She wanted William and Harry to have a normal life and to have fun like other children, so she took them out to the cinema or McDonald's or shopping.

00:05:56.756 --> 00:06:01.630
She did not want them to see only rich people like the royal family.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:08.888
She wanted them to meet people in the normal world too, people with sad and difficult lives.

00:06:08.948 --> 00:06:13.202
She took William to the Passage Day Centre in London.

00:06:13.262 --> 00:06:17.455
The centre was a place for people who live on the streets.

00:06:17.515 --> 00:06:21.598
William met the people there and talked to them.

00:06:21.658 --> 00:06:26.282
William was only a young boy, but he was like Diana.

00:06:26.342 --> 00:06:29.356
He was very good at talking to people.

00:06:29.416 --> 00:06:34.778
Later, Diana took Harry to the center for homeless people too.

00:06:34.838 --> 00:06:40.832
When William and Harry were at home with her, Diana spent a lot of time with them.

00:06:40.892 --> 00:06:44.473
But most of the time they were away at boarding school.

00:06:44.533 --> 00:06:48.345
Then Diana was lonely at home by herself.

00:06:48.404 --> 00:06:53.196
Soon Diana met a new man, Oliver Hall.

00:06:53.256 --> 00:06:56.899
Oliver Hall was very good-looking and popular.

00:06:56.959 --> 00:07:02.303
He knew a lot about art and bought and sold Islamic art.

00:07:02.363 --> 00:07:04.384
He was married.

00:07:04.444 --> 00:07:08.196
Oliver and his wife were friends of Prince Charles.

00:07:08.256 --> 00:07:14.750
Poor and Diana talked to each other on the phone and met at Diana's friend's houses.

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:18.232
Diana was still doing her charity work.

00:07:18.292 --> 00:07:22.515
In March 1993, she visited Nepal.

00:07:22.575 --> 00:07:25.692
In July, she visited Zimbabwe.

00:07:25.752 --> 00:07:29.630
She visited a hospital where there were children with AIDS.

00:07:29.689 --> 00:07:34.744
The children were only five years old, but they had no parents.

00:07:34.804 --> 00:07:37.656
Diana cried when she saw them.

00:07:37.716 --> 00:07:43.190
She went to the countryside and gave food to poor and hungry children.

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:48.454
At home, Diana became interested in women's problems.

00:07:48.514 --> 00:07:55.602
In April 1993, she gave a speech about eating problems in young women.

00:07:55.662 --> 00:07:59.946
The newspapers were still very interested in Diana.

00:08:00.006 --> 00:08:04.828
She had very little private life, and this was very hard for her.

00:08:04.888 --> 00:08:13.102
At a dinner on the 3rd of December, 1993, at the Dorchester Hotel in London, she made a speech.

00:08:13.162 --> 00:08:18.364
She said the newspaper and television reporters made her life very difficult.

00:08:18.424 --> 00:08:22.946
She had no private life and needed more time alone.

00:08:23.006 --> 00:08:26.577
She did not want to do so many things in public.

00:08:26.637 --> 00:08:30.429
She did not want to do so much charity work.

00:08:30.488 --> 00:08:33.870
Oliver Hall left his wife.

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:38.832
But in January 1994, he went back to her.

00:08:38.893 --> 00:08:42.904
He did not want to leave his family for Diana.

00:08:42.965 --> 00:08:49.568
Then in March, James Hewitt gave an interview to a reporter from the Daily Express.

00:08:49.627 --> 00:08:54.863
The newspaper printed the story of Hewitt's relationship with Diana.

00:08:54.923 --> 00:08:59.977
Now the British people knew about Diana's relationship with Hewitt.

00:09:00.037 --> 00:09:05.538
Later that year, Hewitt published a book about his time with Diana.

00:09:05.598 --> 00:09:09.629
The book was called, Princess in Love.

00:09:09.689 --> 00:09:14.740
People already knew about Diana's story from Andrew Morton's book.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.340
They felt very sorry for her.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:20.351
This made Charles very angry.

00:09:20.411 --> 00:09:25.150
So he decided to tell the British people about his life too.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:33.160
He asked a journalist, Jonathan Dimbleby, to write a biography, a book about Charles' life.

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:37.792
He also did an interview with Jonathan Dimbleby on television.

00:09:37.852 --> 00:09:42.374
Many of Charles' friends did not want him to do the interview.

00:09:42.434 --> 00:09:48.938
It is not a good idea for the prince to talk about his personal life on television, they said.

00:09:48.998 --> 00:09:52.862
But Charles did not listen to his friends.

00:09:52.922 --> 00:09:59.216
The interview was on television on the 29th of June 1994.

00:09:59.276 --> 00:10:05.108
Charles talked about the British countryside and about his work with young people.

00:10:05.168 --> 00:10:09.789
But he also talked about a relationship with another woman.

00:10:09.849 --> 00:10:13.640
People thought this woman was Camilla Parker Bowles.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:16.711
Millions of people watched the interview.

00:10:16.771 --> 00:10:19.012
They were very shocked.

00:10:19.072 --> 00:10:41.892
While Charles was married to Diana, he had a girlfriend Seven months later, Andrew and Camilla Parker Bowles divorced.

00:10:41.952 --> 00:10:51.649
Chapter 9 The Road to Divorce Diana went to the United States in October 1994.

00:10:51.709 --> 00:10:55.603
The American people liked her very much.

00:10:55.663 --> 00:10:58.394
Her visit was very successful.

00:10:58.454 --> 00:11:04.666
She met important people like Hillary Clinton and General Colin Powell.

00:11:04.726 --> 00:11:10.088
She talked to Hillary about her children and her plans for the future.

00:11:10.148 --> 00:11:13.220
Soon Diana returned to London.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:16.291
She started her charity work again.

00:11:16.351 --> 00:11:21.367
She visited two special hospitals for people with mental problems.

00:11:21.427 --> 00:11:27.424
Later in 1994, she went to see people in the poor parts of Paris.

00:11:27.484 --> 00:11:35.330
At the end of her visit, the French President, President Mitterrand, gave a dinner for her at the Palace of Versailles.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:38.502
He invited 900 people.

00:11:38.562 --> 00:11:44.316
Diana was not with her husband now, but she had some very good friends.

00:11:44.376 --> 00:11:47.108
These friends helped her a lot.

00:11:47.168 --> 00:11:51.530
One very close friend was Lucia Fletcher de Lima.

00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:58.319
Lucia lived in Washington with her husband, but she spoke to Diana a lot on the telephone.

00:11:58.379 --> 00:12:01.610
She gave Diana advice and helped her.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:11.612
Other good friends were Lady Annabelle Goldsmith, Rosa Monkton, and Carolyn Bartholomew, her old flatmate.

00:12:11.672 --> 00:12:16.574
In 1995, Diana visited 10 countries around the world.

00:12:16.634 --> 00:12:19.674
All of her visits were very successful.

00:12:19.734 --> 00:12:21.806
One was to Japan.

00:12:21.866 --> 00:12:26.017
Diana made a speech to the people in Japanese.

00:12:26.077 --> 00:12:29.528
Later, Diana went to Hong Kong.

00:12:29.588 --> 00:12:35.690
She raised a quarter of a million pounds for charities for young people and for medical work.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:43.222
Diana also went to Italy, France, New York, Russia and Argentina.

00:12:43.282 --> 00:12:48.806
In 1994, Diana made only 10 public visits.

00:12:48.866 --> 00:12:54.851
But in 1995, she made 127.

00:12:54.911 --> 00:12:59.552
Diana's relationship with Oliver Hall was over.

00:12:59.612 --> 00:13:04.603
The newspapers started to write stories about a new male friend.

00:13:04.663 --> 00:13:11.544
This was Will Carling, an English rugby player and captain of the England rugby team.

00:13:11.604 --> 00:13:13.534
People were shocked.

00:13:13.594 --> 00:13:17.209
Diana liked another married man.

00:13:17.269 --> 00:13:24.005
In 1995, Diana met Martin Bashir, a well-known journalist.

00:13:24.065 --> 00:13:29.177
Bashir worked for the BBC's television program, Panorama.

00:13:29.237 --> 00:13:33.278
He wanted Diana to do an interview on television.

00:13:33.338 --> 00:13:39.750
The BBC showed the interview on the 20th of November 1995.

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:43.431
Diana looked beautiful, but sad.

00:13:43.492 --> 00:13:48.278
She wore black clothes and black makeup around her eyes.

00:13:48.338 --> 00:13:53.254
Diana talked about her relationship with Charles and the royal family.

00:13:53.314 --> 00:13:56.464
She talked about Camilla Parker Bowles.

00:13:56.524 --> 00:14:00.695
There were three of us in this marriage, she said.

00:14:00.755 --> 00:14:08.036
She talked about Andrew Morton's book, Her Bellemia, and her relationship with James Hewitt.

00:14:08.096 --> 00:14:12.547
I want to help people with problems, she said.

00:14:12.607 --> 00:14:16.962
Fifteen million people in Britain watch the interview.

00:14:17.022 --> 00:14:21.186
Millions of other people around the world watched it too.

00:14:21.246 --> 00:14:23.226
They were shocked.

00:14:23.286 --> 00:14:27.717
Diana's friends thought the interview was a terrible mistake.

00:14:27.777 --> 00:14:31.237
The royal family were also very upset.

00:14:31.297 --> 00:14:37.418
After the interview, Princess Margaret did not want to be friends with Diana anymore.

00:14:37.478 --> 00:14:43.429
In December 1995, Diana had a letter from the Queen.

00:14:43.489 --> 00:14:47.215
The Queen wanted Charles and Diana to divorce.

00:14:47.275 --> 00:14:51.723
She was worried about her country and the royal family.

00:14:51.783 --> 00:14:59.508
Later, on 15 February 1996, Diana met the Queen at Buckingham Palace.

00:14:59.568 --> 00:15:03.221
I do not want a divorce, said Diana.

00:15:03.281 --> 00:15:05.592
I still love Charles.

00:15:05.652 --> 00:15:12.161
Diana and the Queen talked about William and Harry and about Diana's future.

00:15:12.221 --> 00:15:18.108
Later in February 1996, Diana met with Prince Charles.

00:15:18.168 --> 00:15:21.290
They talked about the end of their marriage.

00:15:21.349 --> 00:15:26.762
On the 28th of August, 1996, they were divorced.

00:15:26.822 --> 00:15:34.946
After the divorce, Diana lost her title, Her Royal Highness, and her special place in the royal family.

00:15:35.006 --> 00:15:39.980
She was now just Diana, Princess of Wales.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:44.572
I never wanted a divorce, Diana wrote.

00:15:44.632 --> 00:15:48.196
I always dreamed of a happy marriage.

00:15:48.256 --> 00:15:53.340
But the fairy tale marriage was over.

00:15:53.400 --> 00:16:13.934
Chapter 10 Starting a New Life Diana was alone, and she had to make a new life for herself.

00:16:13.994 --> 00:16:20.536
She knew many rich and famous people, but she did not only want to spend time with them.

00:16:20.596 --> 00:16:26.408
She wanted a normal life, and she wanted to help the poor and the sick.

00:16:26.468 --> 00:16:34.260
Diana had many beautiful dresses and other clothes, but she did not need these clothes now.

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:37.729
They were from her old life with Prince Charles.

00:16:37.789 --> 00:16:40.448
She did not want to wear them again.

00:16:40.508 --> 00:16:43.620
But she did not know what to do with them.

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:47.092
Then Prince William had a good idea.

00:16:47.152 --> 00:16:51.884
Sell the clothes and make money for charity, he said.

00:16:51.945 --> 00:16:57.017
Christie's, a famous auction house, helped Diana.

00:16:57.077 --> 00:17:02.150
At an auction, a lot of people come to see things that are for sale.

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:07.368
The person who offers the most money for an object can buy it.

00:17:07.428 --> 00:17:15.488
In September 1996, a person from Christie's went to see Diana at Kensington Palace.

00:17:15.549 --> 00:17:19.990
They talked about the sale of Diana's clothes at an auction.

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:23.473
Diana wanted the sale to be in New York.

00:17:23.532 --> 00:17:27.364
She wanted the money to help people with AIDS.

00:17:27.425 --> 00:17:31.776
Diana also wanted to help people in other countries.

00:17:31.836 --> 00:17:35.192
She was very worried about landmines.

00:17:35.252 --> 00:17:39.216
A landmine is a bomb which is put under the ground.

00:17:39.276 --> 00:17:43.327
It explodes when a person or car moves over it.

00:17:43.387 --> 00:17:46.898
Many countries use landmines in wars.

00:17:46.958 --> 00:17:49.819
Landmines are very dangerous.

00:17:49.879 --> 00:17:56.991
People, often women and children, die or lose arms or legs because of landmines.

00:17:57.051 --> 00:18:03.546
Many people did not know about landmines, and Diana wanted to tell the world about them.

00:18:03.606 --> 00:18:08.212
She wanted to stop countries from using landmines in war.

00:18:08.272 --> 00:18:16.958
She talked to the British Red Cross and in January 1997 she went to Angola for the Red Cross.

00:18:17.018 --> 00:18:23.493
There was terrible war in Angola and there were many landmines in that country.

00:18:23.553 --> 00:18:30.310
People who worked for the television company the BBC went with Diana and filmed her.

00:18:30.370 --> 00:18:34.014
She met people with terrible landmine injuries.

00:18:34.074 --> 00:18:38.076
She worked hard and visited dangerous places.

00:18:38.136 --> 00:18:42.300
She walked in parts of the countryside where there were landmines.

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:44.712
But she was not afraid.

00:18:44.772 --> 00:18:50.076
She went to hospitals and talked to children with injuries from landmines.

00:18:50.136 --> 00:18:53.730
She sat with them and held their hands.

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:58.388
Diana also wanted to help people with eating problems.

00:18:58.448 --> 00:19:03.546
In the UK, in May 1997, she made a speech.

00:19:03.606 --> 00:19:07.448
I don't have problems with bulimia anymore, she said.

00:19:07.509 --> 00:19:11.040
Diana looked beautiful and healthy.

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:14.192
Diana was very busy.

00:19:14.252 --> 00:19:23.198
In May, she and Prince William went to lunch with the new British Prime Minister, Tony Blair and his family.

00:19:23.259 --> 00:19:26.506
They talked about Diana's future.

00:19:26.566 --> 00:19:31.615
In June, Diana flew to Washington to meet Hillary Clinton.

00:19:31.675 --> 00:19:35.577
Then she went to New York to meet Mother Teresa.

00:19:35.638 --> 00:19:39.340
She liked Mother Teresa's work very much.

00:19:39.401 --> 00:19:46.646
Later that year, in June, she flew back to New York for a party at Christie's auction house.

00:19:46.706 --> 00:19:50.528
The party was before the sale of Diana's clothes.

00:19:50.588 --> 00:19:54.114
The sale was a great success.

00:19:54.174 --> 00:19:58.138
All Diana's dresses sold for a total of $3,258,750.

00:19:58.178 --> 00:20:00.159
The top price was $222,500 for a dress.

00:20:00.199 --> 00:20:15.908
Diana wore this dress when she danced with John Travolta.

00:20:15.968 --> 00:20:33.058
CHAPTER 11 New love.

00:20:33.118 --> 00:20:37.050
There was a new man in Diana's life.

00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:41.442
Diana knew a woman called Una Shanley to follow.

00:20:41.502 --> 00:20:46.174
Una's husband, Joseph, had a problem with his heart.

00:20:46.234 --> 00:20:50.177
In August 1995, he was very ill.

00:20:50.237 --> 00:20:53.689
He went to the Royal Brompton Hospital in London.

00:20:53.749 --> 00:20:56.492
He had a heart operation.

00:20:56.552 --> 00:21:01.356
On August the 31st, Una telephone Diana.

00:21:01.416 --> 00:21:04.278
Diana went quickly to the hospital.

00:21:04.338 --> 00:21:06.998
She met Joseph's doctors.

00:21:07.058 --> 00:21:10.450
One of them was Hasnut Khan.

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:13.681
Hasnut Khan was from Pakistan.

00:21:13.741 --> 00:21:18.402
He was 36 years old and very good looking.

00:21:18.462 --> 00:21:21.554
Diana often went to the hospital.

00:21:21.614 --> 00:21:24.767
She met Hasnut Khan many times.

00:21:24.827 --> 00:21:28.052
She was very interested in his work.

00:21:28.112 --> 00:21:31.844
Sometimes she watched him doing operations.

00:21:31.904 --> 00:21:35.858
Diana and Hasnad Khan were good friends.

00:21:35.918 --> 00:21:39.961
Soon, they became more than friends.

00:21:40.021 --> 00:21:44.294
Diana often called Hasnad Khan at the hospital.

00:21:44.355 --> 00:21:48.867
But when she called him, she did not use her real name.

00:21:48.928 --> 00:21:53.481
Sometimes she called herself Dr. Armani.

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:59.952
Sometimes Diana and Hasnut Khan had dinner in small restaurants in London.

00:22:00.012 --> 00:22:03.724
But Khan usually came to Kensington Palace.

00:22:03.784 --> 00:22:06.976
Diana was very happy.

00:22:07.036 --> 00:22:11.298
Diana was very much in love with Hasnut Khan.

00:22:11.358 --> 00:22:15.610
Khan cared about people and he saved lives.

00:22:15.670 --> 00:22:17.711
Diana liked this.

00:22:17.771 --> 00:22:23.026
She began reading medical books so she could talk to him about his work.

00:22:23.086 --> 00:22:32.044
Khan was also very kind to her, and he liked Diana the person, not because she was a princess.

00:22:32.104 --> 00:22:43.928
Hasnut Khan's religion was Islam, so Diana also began reading books about Islam, and she became very interested in Pakistan.

00:22:43.988 --> 00:22:55.100
She bought Pakistani women's clothes, Diana's good friend, Lady Annabelle Goldsmith, had a young and beautiful daughter, Jemima.

00:22:55.160 --> 00:23:00.932
Jemima was married to the famous Pakistani cricket player, Imran Khan.

00:23:00.992 --> 00:23:05.544
Imran Khan was interested in Pakistani politics.

00:23:05.604 --> 00:23:12.296
He also had a hospital in Pakistan for people with cancer, a serious illness.

00:23:12.356 --> 00:23:16.568
Diana became very friendly with Jemima Khan.

00:23:16.628 --> 00:23:21.290
She talked to her about marriage to a Pakistani man.

00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:28.276
Diana went to Lahore, Pakistan, in February and May of 1996.

00:23:28.336 --> 00:23:34.102
She visited Jemima and Imran Khan and Imran Khan's hospital.

00:23:34.162 --> 00:23:39.155
She talked to many children with cancer and helped them a lot.

00:23:39.216 --> 00:23:45.064
Many photographs appeared in the newspapers of Diana with sick children.

00:23:45.124 --> 00:23:50.562
At first, Diana and Hasnut's relationship was secret.

00:23:50.622 --> 00:23:54.124
But later the newspapers found out about it.

00:23:54.184 --> 00:23:57.238
Hasnut Khan was very unhappy.

00:23:57.298 --> 00:24:02.042
He did not want the newspapers to write stories about him and Diana.

00:24:02.102 --> 00:24:05.954
He did not want his photograph in all the newspapers.

00:24:06.014 --> 00:24:11.019
He did not want to be famous because he was Diana's lover.

00:24:11.079 --> 00:24:14.160
Diana wanted to marry Khan.

00:24:14.221 --> 00:24:19.354
But the most important thing in Hazenat Khan's life was his work.

00:24:19.414 --> 00:24:25.378
He wanted to be a good doctor and to work in Pakistan, his home country.

00:24:25.438 --> 00:24:29.062
He did not want to be Diana's husband.

00:24:29.122 --> 00:24:32.824
Diana and Khan's relationship finished.

00:24:32.884 --> 00:24:38.860
Diana still wanted to marry him, but she knew that they had no future.

00:24:38.920 --> 00:24:43.488
That same summer, Diana met another man.

00:24:43.548 --> 00:25:06.807
Dodi al-Fayed Chapter 12 The Last Summer Dodi al-Fayed's father was Muhammad al-Fayed.

00:25:06.867 --> 00:25:12.065
Muhammad al-Fayed was Egyptian, and he was very rich.

00:25:12.125 --> 00:25:22.237
He had nine houses, a private plane, a helicopter, many expensive cars, and a film company.

00:25:22.297 --> 00:25:26.789
In 1979, he bought the Ritz Hotel in Paris.

00:25:26.850 --> 00:25:34.134
And in 1984, he bought the most famous shop in London, Harrods.

00:25:34.194 --> 00:25:37.956
Mohammed Al-Fayed liked British people.

00:25:38.016 --> 00:25:41.107
He wanted to be part of British society.

00:25:41.167 --> 00:25:45.798
He wanted famous people like Diana to be his friends.

00:25:45.858 --> 00:25:53.991
So in the summer of 1997, he invited Diana and her sons to stay with him and his family.

00:25:54.051 --> 00:25:59.272
They could stay at his home near Santa Fe, in the south of France.

00:25:59.332 --> 00:26:06.874
Diana had no summer plans for herself and her sons, so she said yes to Muhammad.

00:26:06.934 --> 00:26:11.589
Muhammad bought a beautiful yacht, the Johnnie Carl.

00:26:11.649 --> 00:26:15.004
It cost £15 million.

00:26:15.064 --> 00:26:18.406
16 sailors worked on the boat.

00:26:18.466 --> 00:26:22.048
Mohammed telephoned his son, Dodi.

00:26:22.108 --> 00:26:28.942
At that time, Dodi was in Paris with his fiancé, the woman he planned to marry.

00:26:29.002 --> 00:26:33.546
She was an American model called Kelly Fisher.

00:26:33.606 --> 00:26:39.282
Mohammed told his son to leave Kelly and come and meet Diana.

00:26:39.342 --> 00:26:44.567
On the 14th of July, he sent his private plane to Paris.

00:26:44.627 --> 00:26:48.328
The plane took Dodie to the family villa.

00:26:48.388 --> 00:26:52.380
Dodie fired was 42 years old.

00:26:52.440 --> 00:26:55.031
He had the life of a playboy.

00:26:55.091 --> 00:27:02.224
His father gave him lots of money and he spent it on having fun and driving fast cars.

00:27:02.284 --> 00:27:09.008
He was also successful with women because he was good looking and kind.

00:27:09.068 --> 00:27:16.685
On the 16th of July, Diana and the boys flew in Muhammad's private plane to France.

00:27:16.746 --> 00:27:24.142
They stayed in his villa, the Castel Santelan, and spent time on his yacht.

00:27:24.202 --> 00:27:28.766
The photographers followed Diana to the south of France.

00:27:28.827 --> 00:27:32.320
They waited in boats near Muhammad's villa.

00:27:32.380 --> 00:27:38.650
They took pictures of Diana by the swimming pool and having fun in the sea.

00:27:38.711 --> 00:27:45.019
The photographers saw Dodie with Diana, but they did not know who he was.

00:27:45.079 --> 00:27:47.650
They thought he was a sailor from the John A.

00:27:47.670 --> 00:27:48.790
Carl.

00:27:48.850 --> 00:27:56.474
They did not know he was Muhammad al-Fayed son, but they saw that Diana looked very happy.

00:27:56.534 --> 00:28:03.306
Kelly Fisher, Dodie's fiance saw photos of Diana and Dodie in the newspapers.

00:28:03.366 --> 00:28:05.467
She was very angry.

00:28:05.527 --> 00:28:08.415
She called Dodie, but he did not answer.

00:28:08.475 --> 00:28:12.304
so she telephoned Dodie's father, Muhammad.

00:28:12.364 --> 00:28:16.596
But Diana was more important for Muhammad than Kelly.

00:28:16.656 --> 00:28:23.448
Forget about Dodie, Muhammad told her, you and Dodie are finished.

00:28:23.509 --> 00:28:26.610
Diana wrote a letter to Dodie.

00:28:26.670 --> 00:28:29.972
She thanked him for a wonderful holiday together.

00:28:30.032 --> 00:28:38.356
Darling Dodie, she wrote, thank you for the most magical six days on the ocean waves.

00:28:38.416 --> 00:28:43.828
On the 20th of July, Diana flew back to London.

00:28:43.888 --> 00:28:46.629
There she met Hasnut Khan.

00:28:46.689 --> 00:28:49.870
But their relationship was finished.

00:28:49.930 --> 00:28:54.271
In late July, Diana flew back to Paris.

00:28:54.331 --> 00:28:56.132
She met Dodi for a day.

00:28:56.152 --> 00:29:02.163
On the 31st of July, she flew back to the Johnacal.

00:29:02.223 --> 00:29:05.434
William and Harry were not with her this time.

00:29:05.494 --> 00:29:09.528
They were on holiday with Prince Charles in Scotland.

00:29:09.588 --> 00:29:15.384
Diana and Dodi went to Corsica and Sardinia on the Johnacal.

00:29:15.444 --> 00:29:19.106
Diana was very happy and relaxed.

00:29:19.166 --> 00:29:23.240
But the photographers followed them and took photos.

00:29:23.300 --> 00:29:28.733
The newspapers in London paid a lot of money for these photos.

00:29:28.793 --> 00:29:35.096
On the 8th of August, Diana went to Bosnia to talk about landmines.

00:29:35.156 --> 00:29:40.814
She visited Sarajevo and met people with injuries from landmines.

00:29:40.874 --> 00:29:46.084
Then she went on holiday to Greece with her friend, Rosa Monkton.

00:29:46.144 --> 00:29:50.587
But Diana and Dodie spent time together too in August.

00:29:50.648 --> 00:29:54.640
They stayed together in London and on the Johnacal.

00:29:54.701 --> 00:29:57.964
The photographers were there all the time.

00:29:58.024 --> 00:30:02.788
They came when Diana and Dodie had a romantic walk on a beach.

00:30:02.848 --> 00:30:06.680
They flew in helicopters over the Johnacal.

00:30:06.740 --> 00:30:11.902
On the 30th of August, Diana and Dodie went to Paris.

00:30:11.962 --> 00:30:15.304
But the photographers found out their plans.

00:30:15.365 --> 00:30:18.737
The photographers waited for them at the airport.

00:30:18.797 --> 00:30:23.920
They followed their car on motorbikes, trying to take photographs.

00:30:23.980 --> 00:30:28.793
Diana and Dodie went to Dodie's apartment to dress for dinner.

00:30:28.853 --> 00:30:34.106
The photographers waited outside the apartment, shouting and pushing.

00:30:34.166 --> 00:30:36.307
Dodie was angry.

00:30:36.367 --> 00:30:42.240
When Diana and Dodi came out of the apartment, the photographers were still there.

00:30:42.300 --> 00:30:46.502
They got on their bikes and drove very near the car.

00:30:46.562 --> 00:30:49.324
It was very dangerous.

00:30:49.384 --> 00:30:55.611
A table was reserved for dinner at a restaurant called Che Benoit.

00:30:55.671 --> 00:30:59.646
But Dodi did not want the photographers to follow them there.

00:30:59.706 --> 00:31:05.380
So he changed their plans and decided to have dinner at the Ritz hotel.

00:31:05.440 --> 00:31:07.630
They drove to the Ritz.

00:31:07.690 --> 00:31:10.522
But the photographers were there too.

00:31:10.582 --> 00:31:14.433
Diana got out of the car and ran inside.

00:31:14.494 --> 00:31:18.896
Dodi and Diana had dinner upstairs in the Ritz.

00:31:18.956 --> 00:31:23.789
At dinner, Dodi made a plan to lose the photographers.

00:31:23.849 --> 00:31:32.106
Dodi's car was at the front door of the hotel, but Dodi decided to use another car at the back door.

00:31:32.166 --> 00:31:35.848
The photographers did not know about this car.

00:31:35.908 --> 00:31:41.592
The assistant head of security at the Ritz was called Henri Paul.

00:31:41.653 --> 00:31:45.535
Dodi told Henri Paul about his plan.

00:31:45.595 --> 00:31:49.278
He wanted him to drive the secret car.

00:31:49.338 --> 00:31:53.173
Diana and Dodi left by the back door.

00:31:53.233 --> 00:32:00.108
Trevor Reese Jones, a man who worked for the fires and protected Diana, went to.

00:32:00.168 --> 00:32:03.720
Dodie sat in the back behind Henri Paul.

00:32:03.780 --> 00:32:06.830
Diana was on Dodie's right side.

00:32:06.890 --> 00:32:09.952
Nobody in the car wore a seatbelt.

00:32:10.012 --> 00:32:15.054
At about midnight, Paul drove quickly away from the hotel.

00:32:15.114 --> 00:32:18.384
But the photographers soon saw the car.

00:32:18.444 --> 00:32:22.894
Quickly they got onto their motorbikes and followed it.

00:32:22.954 --> 00:32:26.936
Henri Paul tried to lose the photographers.

00:32:26.996 --> 00:32:32.972
He did not take the direct road, the Champs-Elysé, back to Dodie's apartment.

00:32:33.032 --> 00:32:37.805
He decided to drive down the tunnel under the plastama.

00:32:37.865 --> 00:32:44.411
Henri Paul was driving too fast, and he had alcohol in his body.

00:32:44.471 --> 00:32:51.862
Only three minutes after leaving the Ritz hotel, the car crashed into part of the tunnel.

00:32:51.923 --> 00:32:55.340
Dodi and Paul were killed.

00:32:55.400 --> 00:33:00.665
But Trevor Reese-Jones and Diana were still alive.

00:33:00.726 --> 00:33:08.643
About 10 to 15 photographers arrived in seconds and started taking photographs of Diana.

00:33:08.703 --> 00:33:13.027
Only two of them called for help on their mobile phones.

00:33:13.087 --> 00:33:18.733
People were very shocked because the photographers did not help the people in the car.

00:33:18.794 --> 00:33:24.418
When the police arrived, they arrested seven of the photographers.

00:33:24.478 --> 00:33:29.650
A doctor, Frederic Malier, was in the tunnel.

00:33:29.711 --> 00:33:32.592
He tried to help Diana.

00:33:32.652 --> 00:33:39.946
Diana did not look badly hurt, but the injuries inside her body were terrible.

00:33:40.006 --> 00:33:42.768
The ambulances arrived.

00:33:42.828 --> 00:33:46.992
They took Diana to La Pitea's Salpatria Hospital.

00:33:47.052 --> 00:33:50.024
but the doctors there could not save her.

00:33:50.084 --> 00:33:51.494
At 4 a.m.

00:33:51.554 --> 00:33:58.966
Paris time, on the morning of the 31st of August 1997, Diana died.

00:33:59.027 --> 00:34:04.798
The British ambassador in Paris, Sir Michael J, came to the hospital.

00:34:04.858 --> 00:34:11.480
He telephoned the Queen's assistant private secretary, Sir Robin Janvrin, in London.

00:34:11.540 --> 00:34:14.884
Diana is dead, he said.

00:34:14.944 --> 00:34:24.168
Janverin told the Queen and Prince Philip.

00:34:24.229 --> 00:34:42.592
Chapter 13 The People's Princess People all over the world heard the sad and terrible news, but nobody could believe it.

00:34:42.652 --> 00:34:45.146
How could Diana be dead?

00:34:45.206 --> 00:34:47.782
It could not be true.

00:34:47.842 --> 00:34:55.488
Prince's William and Harry were at Balmoral in Scotland, with Prince Charles and the Queen and Prince Philip.

00:34:55.548 --> 00:34:59.742
Prince Charles told them about their mother's death.

00:34:59.802 --> 00:35:03.634
Tony Blair was the new British Prime Minister.

00:35:03.694 --> 00:35:09.699
The morning after Diana's death, he spoke about Diana and the British people.

00:35:09.760 --> 00:35:11.721
They liked her.

00:35:11.781 --> 00:35:15.950
They loved her as one of the people, he said.

00:35:16.010 --> 00:35:25.050
She was the people's princess, and that's how she will stay, in all our hearts and memories forever.

00:35:25.110 --> 00:35:31.544
Prince Charles and Diana's two sisters, Sarah and Jane, flew to Paris.

00:35:31.604 --> 00:35:35.186
They brought Diana's body back to London.

00:35:35.246 --> 00:35:45.715
Sarah wanted a quiet funeral for Diana at the Spencer family home in Allthorp, but thousands of people waited by the road from the airport.

00:35:45.775 --> 00:35:50.071
There was not going to be a quiet funeral.

00:35:50.131 --> 00:35:55.795
Diana's body was taken to the Chapel Royal at St. James's Palace.

00:35:55.856 --> 00:35:59.579
Then it was taken to Kensington Palace.

00:35:59.639 --> 00:36:04.762
Charles Spencer, Diana's brother, lived in South Africa.

00:36:04.822 --> 00:36:07.966
He flew to London immediately.

00:36:08.026 --> 00:36:14.080
Diana's mother Francis was at her home in Scotland on the Isle of Sile.

00:36:14.140 --> 00:36:16.733
She too came to London.

00:36:16.793 --> 00:36:21.215
But the royal family was still at Balmoral on holiday.

00:36:21.275 --> 00:36:24.736
The British people began to ask questions.

00:36:24.796 --> 00:36:28.848
Why aren't the royal family here in London, they said?

00:36:28.908 --> 00:36:30.418
Do they care?

00:36:30.478 --> 00:36:34.019
Said one popular British newspaper, The Sun.

00:36:34.079 --> 00:36:37.660
Where is the queen when the country needs her?

00:36:37.720 --> 00:36:42.112
Why doesn't the queen talk to the British people about Diana?

00:36:42.172 --> 00:36:44.099
Ask the people.

00:36:44.159 --> 00:36:47.758
People began to dislike the royal family.

00:36:47.819 --> 00:36:54.053
The royal family was cold and did not care about Diana, they said.

00:36:54.113 --> 00:37:00.798
People said these things, but still the queen and the royal family stayed in Scotland.

00:37:00.859 --> 00:37:05.572
People put flowers outside the gates of Kensington Palace.

00:37:05.632 --> 00:37:09.394
The number of flowers grew and grew.

00:37:09.455 --> 00:37:13.452
People wrote cards and left messages for Diana.

00:37:13.512 --> 00:37:19.159
They waited for hours to sign a special book to remember Diana.

00:37:19.220 --> 00:37:27.052
Then at last, on Friday the 5th of September, the royal family returned to London.

00:37:27.112 --> 00:37:32.625
The Queen made a speech and the family walked in the streets with the people.

00:37:32.685 --> 00:37:38.038
Finally, they began to understand the feelings of the people.

00:37:38.098 --> 00:37:43.672
Diana's funeral was on the 6th of September 1997.

00:37:43.732 --> 00:37:51.518
More than one million people came to London, and many more watched the funeral on television.

00:37:51.578 --> 00:37:58.880
Prince William and Prince Harry walked behind Diana's coffin, the box where her body was.

00:37:58.940 --> 00:38:03.652
Diana's favourite white flowers were on top of the coffin.

00:38:03.712 --> 00:38:10.174
Prince Harry, who was only 12 years old, wrote one word on a card.

00:38:10.234 --> 00:38:12.502
The word was mummy.

00:38:12.562 --> 00:38:15.694
This card was on the coffin too.

00:38:15.754 --> 00:38:20.590
When people saw the card, they felt very sad.

00:38:20.650 --> 00:38:26.546
The coffin went from Kensington Palace to Westminster Abbey for the funeral.

00:38:26.607 --> 00:38:30.632
Thousands of people stood quietly by the road.

00:38:30.692 --> 00:38:33.221
Many people cried.

00:38:33.281 --> 00:38:38.390
Famous people from all over the world came to the funeral service.

00:38:38.450 --> 00:38:41.280
Bill and Hillary Clinton came.

00:38:41.341 --> 00:38:46.742
There were actors like Tom Cruise, Tom Hanks and Nicole Kidman.

00:38:46.803 --> 00:38:51.904
There were singers like Sting, Elton John and George Michael.

00:38:51.964 --> 00:39:00.666
There were Diana's old school friends like Carolyn Bartholomew and her old head mistress from West Heath School.

00:39:00.726 --> 00:39:05.929
There were Diana's new friends, like Lucia Fletcher de Lima.

00:39:05.990 --> 00:39:10.644
Hasnut Khan was there, and Imran Khan and Jemima.

00:39:10.704 --> 00:39:14.588
And there were many people from Diana's charities.

00:39:14.648 --> 00:39:20.043
Elton John sang a beautiful song, Candle in the Wind.

00:39:20.103 --> 00:39:26.158
He first wrote it for Marilyn Monroe, but wrote new words for Diana.

00:39:26.218 --> 00:39:34.003
Diana and Marilyn Monroe died at exactly the same age, 36.

00:39:34.063 --> 00:39:39.147
Diana's brother Charles made a speech at the funeral.

00:39:39.207 --> 00:39:43.790
Diana's name means Huntress, he said.

00:39:43.850 --> 00:39:48.344
But Diana became the most hunted woman in the world.

00:39:48.404 --> 00:39:52.256
Outside, thousands of people listened.

00:39:52.317 --> 00:39:57.119
When Charles finished, they began to clap their hands.

00:39:57.179 --> 00:40:03.959
After the funeral, the coffin went very slowly to Althorp, the Spencer family home.

00:40:04.019 --> 00:40:07.770
People in the streets of London threw flowers.

00:40:07.830 --> 00:40:13.811
At Althorp, Charles Spencer said, Diana is home.

00:40:13.871 --> 00:40:19.212
Diana is now buried in the ground on a small island.

00:40:19.272 --> 00:40:23.872
The island is in a lake in the garden at Althorp.

00:40:23.932 --> 00:40:27.378
There are trees all around the lake.

00:40:27.438 --> 00:40:38.020
It is the perfect place for a princess at peace.

00:40:38.080 --> 00:41:02.658
Chapter 14 After Diana's death The Diana Princess of Wales Memorial Fund The Diana Princess of Wales Memorial Fund was started on the 14th of September 1997.

00:41:02.718 --> 00:41:07.962
When it began, there was 19 million pounds in the fund.

00:41:08.022 --> 00:41:13.928
Money that Diana left and money from Prince Charles was put into the fund.

00:41:13.988 --> 00:41:23.415
Money from the people of Britain and money from the sales of Sir Elton John's song Candle in the Wind was also put in.

00:41:23.475 --> 00:41:27.777
The fund gives money to people for three reasons.

00:41:27.838 --> 00:41:36.124
The first reason is to stop the use of landmines and to help people hurt by landmines.

00:41:36.184 --> 00:41:44.370
The second is to help people in Africa who are dying from an illness, for example, AIDS.

00:41:44.430 --> 00:41:52.460
The third is to give money to help young people in the UK with special difficulties.

00:41:52.520 --> 00:42:00.528
The President of the Fund is Lady Sarah McCorkidale, Diana's oldest sister.

00:42:00.588 --> 00:42:11.351
Charles and Camilla Prince Charles married Camilla Parker Bowles on the 9th of April 2005.

00:42:11.411 --> 00:42:17.633
After the wedding, the Queen gave a party for Charles and Camilla at Windsor Castle.

00:42:17.693 --> 00:42:21.036
Later Charles and Camilla went to Scotland.

00:42:21.096 --> 00:42:27.072
Camilla's title is now Her Royal Highness, The Duchess of Cornwall.

00:42:27.132 --> 00:42:32.625
Sometimes Charles and Camilla carry out royal duties together.

00:42:32.685 --> 00:42:46.624
On the 1st of July 2007, about 10 years after Princess Diana died, there was a concert for her in London.

00:42:46.684 --> 00:42:50.667
The 1st of July was Diana's birthday.

00:42:50.727 --> 00:42:54.609
Prince William and Prince Harry planned the concert.

00:42:54.669 --> 00:43:00.270
They invited many of the world's most famous singers and entertainers to come there.

00:43:00.330 --> 00:43:11.652
They invited Sir Elton John, the English National Ballet, Brian Ferry, Andrea Bocelli, Rod Stewart, and take that.

00:43:11.712 --> 00:43:16.852
The concert was eight hours long and was very successful.

00:43:16.912 --> 00:43:24.394
People in 140 countries watched the concert on television or heard it on the radio.

00:43:24.455 --> 00:43:30.128
63,000 people came to Wembley Stadium to see the concert.

00:43:30.188 --> 00:43:35.190
At the end, a video of Diana as a child was shown.

00:43:35.250 --> 00:43:39.982
The music for the video was the song by the pop group Queen.

00:43:40.042 --> 00:43:43.274
These are the days of our lives.

00:43:43.334 --> 00:43:47.275
There is now a DVD of the concert.

00:43:47.336 --> 00:43:54.237
The money from the concert went to charities chosen by Prince William and Prince Harry.

00:43:54.297 --> 00:44:04.679
The charities were the Diana Princess of Wales Memorial Fund, Centrepoint Charity for the Homeless and Centre Barley.

00:44:04.739 --> 00:44:14.742
A charity started in April 2006 by Prince Harry and Prince Ciosio of Rosoto, a small country in South Africa.

00:44:14.802 --> 00:44:19.544
This charity helps children and young people in Lusoto.

00:44:19.605 --> 00:44:25.049
There are many children in Lusoto whose parents have died of AIDS.

00:44:25.109 --> 00:44:30.142
Diana is dead, but her memory lives on.

00:44:30.202 --> 00:44:36.266
People all around the world still want to see photographs and read books about her.

00:44:36.326 --> 00:44:46.346
They still want to know about the beautiful and caring princess who touched people's hearts all over the world.

00:44:46.406 --> 00:44:47.778
Oh Oh

